## gtk-rs glib crate 0.18.5 compatibility backport

The desktop workspace retains the MIT-licensed `glib` 0.18.5 source at
`desktop/vendor/glib-0.18.5-rustsec-2024-0429` to apply the upstream correction
for RUSTSEC-2024-0429 without replacing the GTK3 dependency graph.
The retained source also corrects safe-API memory invariants in inline
boxed slices, StrV termination, foreign GString byte lengths and LogField value
lifetimes, linked-list retention and borrowed container copying. Additional local
corrections cover thread-affine destruction and results, empty-container
conversion, single-view Unicode extents, URI pointer ranges, extension unwind,
retained Variant owners, and rejected parameter or Variant construction inputs.
Their provenance and native-test boundary are recorded in BACKPORT.md.

- Upstream project: <https://github.com/gtk-rs/gtk-rs-core>
- Upstream correction: <https://github.com/gtk-rs/gtk-rs-core/pull/1343>
- Registry archive SHA-256: `233daaf6e83ae6a12a52055f568f9d7cf4671dabb78ff9560ab6da230ce00ee5`
- Copyrights are retained by the gtk-rs contributors, as stated in the retained
  `COPYRIGHT` file. The complete MIT permission and warranty terms remain in
  the retained `LICENSE` file.
- `BACKPORT.md` records the source change and qualification boundary. The
  version remains 0.18.5; source verification remains separate from scanner
  matching and release qualification.

The retained `SHA256SUMS` inventories every upstream file and `BACKPORT.md`.
Run `python3 scripts/verify_glib_backport.py` to validate the retained file set,
source digests, correction and Cargo resolution. This source check reports the
known advisory explicitly; it does not run or waive vulnerability scanning.

## Project Nayuki qrcodegen crate 1.8.0

ShellX Drive uses the Project Nayuki `qrcodegen` Rust crate to generate the
two-factor-authentication setup QR module matrix on the server. No vendored
browser QR encoder ships with this source tree.

- Project URL: <https://www.nayuki.io/page/qr-code-generator-library>
- crates.io package: `qrcodegen` version `1.8.0`
- Cargo.lock source: `registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index`
- Cargo.lock package checksum: `4339fc7a1021c9c1621d87f5e3505f2805c8c105420ba2f2a4df86814590c142`
- License: MIT

### Registry/Cargo.lock reproducibility

`Cargo.toml` allows compatible updates from `qrcodegen = "1.8"`. Cargo resolves
that package through the crates.io registry, and `Cargo.lock` records the exact
version, registry source and package checksum above. `cargo build --locked`
refuses a changed resolution, while Cargo verifies the downloaded package
against the locked checksum. This NOTICE is included in Cargo package inputs
and in the server binary support archive; run the focused public-documentation
and packaging tests after changing this dependency or notice.

